# Coinbase Advanced API (required for trading) - ALL KEYS IN .env ONLY
# IMPORTANT: Never put secrets in repo. .env is gitignored. 
# COINBASE_API_SECRET holds the full PEM EC private key content (multiline supported).
# No file paths or cb_key.pem - keys exclusively via environment variables.
COINBASE_API_KEY=your_key_here
COINBASE_API_SECRET=your_pem_private_key_content_here

# Telegram Reporting (optional)
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=

# OpenRouter / LLM keys (if using external models)
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Apify (sentiment scraping)
APIFY_API_KEY=

# Optional: override rebalance time
DAILY_REBALANCE_TIME=09:00

# Coinbase Developer Platform (CDP) / AgentKit keys (for CdpEvmWalletProvider, on-chain actions, enhanced balance views)
# Obtain from: https://portal.cdp.coinbase.com/
# Steps to obtain (this P0 task):
# 1. Visit https://portal.cdp.coinbase.com and sign in (or create account; free tier OK for PoC/tests).
# 2. Create a new Project if none exists.
# 3. Navigate to API Keys (or Settings > API Keys) and create a CDP API Key.
#    - Record the "Key ID" (use as CDP_API_KEY_ID) and the full Secret (CDP_API_KEY_SECRET).
# 4. For wallet features: Generate a "Wallet Secret" (look under Wallets > Non-custodial or Security in portal).
#    Reference: https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/get-started/docs/cdp-api-keys
#    and https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/wallets/quickstart/api-key-auth
# 5. (Optional) Set NETWORK_ID (base-sepolia for test, base or ethereum for main).
#    Defaults to base-sepolia in the lib.
#
# Add these to your real .env (gitignored):
CDP_API_KEY_ID=your-cdp-api-key-id-here
CDP_API_KEY_SECRET=your-cdp-api-key-secret-here
CDP_WALLET_SECRET=your-cdp-wallet-secret-here
# NETWORK_ID=base-sepolia
#
# These 3 are REQUIRED to successfully init CdpEvmWalletProvider / CdpApiActionProvider without the "Missing required environment variables" error.
# 
# IMPORTANT NOTES:
# - CDP keys enable *Coinbase Developer Platform non-custodial on-chain wallets* (EVM chains like Base, Solana).
# - They are SEPARATE from your Coinbase Advanced Trade CEX API keys (used for spot trading on exchange).
# - AgentKit + CDP will report on-chain wallet balances/holdings for wallets you create/fund via CDP.
# - For CEX spot "live holdings" comparison: the test will still use exchange_client for CEX view; CDP provides an independent on-chain view or additional data (may differ or be empty if no on-chain activity).
# - Goal of re-broaden: once keys set, init real providers, call get_balance / get_wallet_details / actions, measure latency vs exchange_client.get_crypto_available + holdings, check accuracy on assets held.
#
# Prod note: For production, ensure this .env (or loaded equivalent) has live keys.
# Verify with: python -c "import os; print('KEYS LOADED' if os.getenv('COINBASE_API_KEY') else 'MISSING')"
# CDP verify: python -c "import os; print('CDP KEYS LOADED' if os.getenv('CDP_API_KEY_ID') else 'MISSING CDP')"
